---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
---
<Base title="Editorial policy" description="How Southwala sources, writes, checks and corrects stories.">
  <div class="page">
    <h1>Editorial policy</h1>
    <h2>Sources</h2><p>We build on reporting by established outlets, official statements, court records and public posts. Every story links its sources under "Receipts". We explain stories in our own words and never copy text.</p>
    <h2>Accuracy</h2><p>We only state what our sources support, attribute claims to whoever made them, and say plainly when something is unconfirmed. Allegations against named people are reported as allegations, never as fact.</p>
    <h2>AI disclosure</h2><p>We use AI tools to research and draft stories. Our bylines are AI-assisted desk voices and are labelled as such on every story and on our <a href="/team/">team page</a>. They never claim interviews, field reporting or personal experience. A human editor owns the final call, and politically sensitive stories are reviewed before publication.</p>
    <h2>Opinion and satire</h2><p>Analysis and opinion are labelled. We do not publish fabricated quotes or fake events presented as news.</p>
    <h2>Corrections</h2><p>Found a mistake? Write to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. We fix errors quickly and note the correction with an "Updated" date on the story.</p>
    <h2>Independence</h2><p>No party, politician or studio pays for coverage. Sponsored or affiliate content, when it exists, is clearly labelled.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
